Z||000000||Rare87GT||12-25-2001||04:35 PM||||Im upgrading my suspension. I plan on getting KYB Gas-A-Just Shock Frnt ($29 each) and KYB GR-2 Strut Rear($52 each). I also plan on getting Eibach Lowering Springs, but I need to know of a place that has the 1.5-2" drop not the .8" drop like I saw at Tirerack.com where I am getting my Shocks/Struts. Also is there anything else I would need to upgrade when I am getting all this new suspension stuff. Let me know. Thank you.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Maroon)*5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||G-Nasty||12-26-2001||01:52 AM||||I tried to get KYB GR-2 struts to replace my Bilsteins from J.C. Whitney. They sent wrong parts but its my belief KYB doesn't make an adjustable strut for the fiero...just NON adjust. They have app for firebird not fiero. Also loose the R and HR rated tires and small rims. ZR rated Yokahomas/Dunlop/Falken tires will provide better handling @ higher speeds.<BR>Suspension Techniques/ Beltech / Eibach / West Coast all have nice upgrades.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||12-26-2001||10:27 AM||||The KYB GR-2 struts aren't adjustable.  The AGX are the adjustable ones, and they don't make them for Fieros.  Not that I've been able to find, anyway.||||reg||1
